            },
            {
              "line_number": 1190,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0004\">ADR-0004</a>, <a href=\"#adr-0016\">ADR-0016</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1198,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0003\">ADR-0003</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1206,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0002\">ADR-0002</a>, <a href=\"#adr-0017\">ADR-0017</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1214,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0019\">ADR-0019</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1222,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0010\">ADR-0010</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1235,
              "content": "  <p>Large monorepos fail when “everything depends on everything.” NVide uses four visibility tiers. Enforced by crate features, <code>pub(crate)</code> discipline, and CI dependency allowlists. See <a href=\"#adr-0011\">ADR-0011</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1310,
              "content": "  <p>Multiple version clocks exist on purpose. Do not conflate product release with plugin ABI. See <a href=\"#adr-0015\">ADR-0015</a>, <a href=\"#adr-0010\">ADR-0010</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1517,
              "content": "  <p>Rust correctness at IDE scale depends on explicit ownership. Default: <strong>one owner, many borrowed readers, Arc only at process/service boundaries</strong>. See <a href=\"#adr-0012\">ADR-0012</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1605,
              "content": "  <p>Unify failure handling early so contributors do not invent per-crate conventions. See <a href=\"#adr-0013\">ADR-0013</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1757,
              "content": "    <p>NVide is a <strong>multi-process, message-oriented IDE</strong>. The GUI process is thin; durable state and language intelligence live in workers. Communication uses a versioned binary RPC (Cap’n Proto or similar; see <a href=\"#multiprocess\">Multi-Process / IPC</a>, <a href=\"#adr-0002\">ADR-0002</a>) over local IPC (Unix domain sockets / named pipes) and over the remote transport when the workspace is remote.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1941,
              "content": "    <p>See also <a href=\"#crate-ownership\">Crate Ownership</a>, <a href=\"#dependency-diagram\">Dependency Diagram</a>, and <a href=\"#adr-0011\">ADR-0011</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 2073,
              "content": "        <dt>Status</dt><dd>Accepted (<a href=\"#adr-0003\">ADR-0003</a>)</dd>"
            },
